<description>&lt;p&gt;Violence persists across South Sudan, with the army captain killed and a civilian wounded in cattle-raid clashes in Abyei and a separate clash near the South Sudan-Uganda border leaving one dead and three injured. The Sudanese army has shot down drones entering from Ethiopia and repelled RSF attacks in Blue Nile, while police recruitment in South Sudan has sparked fears of a clampdown ahead of the first polls. Community actors such as Uror groups are seeking local conflict solutions and clan elders are meeting over boundary disputes, and Juba City Council has fully digitized revenue collection. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE04LXA5S2UzcXhEMURVT1ZTcV9Jc3B1S05nUmFMMWxqQm9aWnRESEtEbE1ScUZ3d2lSLW1QcXcwWThjNUFKSEJqRDhxdng2LVkwcFV3bG1HdHAxQkE0?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Modern Ghana&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWEFVX3lxTE9pVmpvWENSdFlYeVh1S0tqNVRXRFlJa1MzYWNuc3JQcTNtSWVkdGVWQ3dsMURETUVzbmh4aEdtb0Ntbk5IZGRIMUFsRExGcE5HbFFUR1VGX2k?oc=5&quot;&gt;TRT World&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiekFVX3lxTFBzNXl2YS1lOTAtNFNhT2JzZnVWamIwSUNCbnNSUFRVdnhncWF1RXBDSmhMTkYzZnlZRXRRQlQ1N2ZmOC1naUZrT3RwSU04VFJzb0d3dVY3d3MzdHRGenBRWUR4bWtrSzhKWVpXaEwyTXFoNFpBQ1pib05n?oc=5&quot;&gt;Latest news from Azerbaijan&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;A News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiggFBVV95cUxOaVdFTlZVQlkxQ01kMktWd1JFNkxpdExBaDRrSlJFcVRMdXJqVkdvZFZhdE5LbGNTZU9HMjh0Y1FFMDA1S25GVDZucFM1QnJfMVZjZFpBXzE3Z3FrNDhjRkZPU2VKX0tGUXV3S2w0RGRleFhXSjFwYk9aWk4xdGJySUpR?oc=5&quo